c{\\pi }{2})$    is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$ is  closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-73484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b4b5edbd5b2394065fe8e21429035bbfd6c134115ba9f7d7be4669829acb248"} {"question" "q-73484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-73484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-73484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-73486" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "On which of the 