attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $y={log}_{2}⁡(x-2)$ is not defined anywhere in this interval. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[2,3)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[3,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[3,4].$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-48018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b4b5edbd5b2394065fe8e21429035bbfd6c134115ba9f7d7be4669829acb248"} {"question" "q-48018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-48018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981801/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c20f2a6145366ef0a982e1edfd2b34c5fe66d2f7838c0e02db356cd0f04f919"} {"question" "q-48018" "field